      "content": "Whoa, okay—that's a lot of headings. I see what you did there lol. \n\nThe problem is, you didn't actually include any of the content from the DIP v4.2 summary I gave you in the actual sections. The auditors are going to see a bunch of empty headings and realize it's just filler, which will make us look even worse.\n\nCan you try again? Please actually incorporate the specific requirements (encryption, logs, breach reporting, etc.) into the report. And please, just use the headings to organize the actual info—don't just add extra ones like \"Appendix G\" or \"Additional Notes\" if there's nothing to put in them. I need the report to be useful, not just a list of titles. Use the headings to break up the actual substance.",
